    "text": "We habba\u00f0 nu ges\u00e6d, swa we sceortlicost mihton, on \u00feam \u00e6rran cwyde, hu se \u00e6lmihtiga God his agen\nNu wylle we git secgan sum \u00f0ing be \u00f0am folce.\nSyx hund \u00feusend manna, swa swa Moyses awrat, w\u00e6ron on \u00fe\u00e6re fyrde, wigendra manna, buton \u00feam\n\u00d0\u00e6t is swutellice to secgenne \u00fe\u00e6t se mete awende, on \u00fe\u00e6s mannes mu\u00f0e \u00fee \u00feone mete \u00e6t, to \u00fe\u00e6s metes\nAnd of heardum stane him arn w\u00e6teres stream him eallum genoh, and eac heora orue, for \u00fean \u00f0e se\nGod sylf com \u00f0a sume d\u00e6g him to on anum mycclum munte \u00fee menn hata\u00f0 Sinai, swa \u00fe\u00e6t eall \u00fe\u00e6t folc\nHe gesette \u00fea \u00e6 eallum \u00feam folce, \u00fe\u00e6t synd rihte lagu, hu men lybban sceoldon, and \u00e6nne God\nHe worhte feala wundra on \u00f0am westene \u00fea, ac \u00fe\u00e6t folc w\u00e6s wi\u00f0err\u00e6de witodlice to oft, and to swy\u00f0e\nMoyses wunode on \u00feam munte mid Gode feowertig daga on an, and \u00fe\u00e6t folc \u00fea hwile worhton him god\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 God to Moyse on \u00feam munte Sinai, Astih adune hra\u00f0e of \u00f0ysum steapum munte; \u00feis folc\nMoyses \u00fea astah of \u00feam sticolan munte, and com to \u00f0am folce \u00e6tforan \u00feam gode, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea sona eode eall seo m\u00e6g\u00f0 him to of Leuies cynne, and he cw\u00e6\u00f0 him \u00fea to, Ga\u00f0 nu hra\u00f0e ealle\n\u00d0a eode seo m\u00e6g\u00f0 be Moyses h\u00e6se \u00feurh ealne \u00feone here \u00e6fre ofsleande, and hi ofslogon on \u00feam d\u00e6ge\nEft \u00e6fter \u00feysum hi begunnon ceorian mid mycelre murcnunge ongean God \u00c6lmihtigne, for heora\n\u00d0a clypodon hi ealle endemes to Moysen, and Moyses geb\u00e6d \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan God for \u00f0am dyrstigan\n\u00d0as race we secga\u00f0 eow nu to rihtinge, \u00fe\u00e6t nan mann ne sceole ceorian ongean God mid dyrstigum\nHi ongunnon eft ceorian and swy\u00f0e murcnian, \u00e6fter fl\u00e6scmettum swy\u00f0e oflyste, and s\u00e6don him\nWitodlice we w\u00e6ron wel on Egipta lande on fisce and on fugele, and on feala estmettum; nu we naht ne\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 Moyses micclum astyred, ac God him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00fe\u00e6t him cuman sceolde, eallum \u00feam folce, na\nGod sende him \u00f0a sona, mid swy\u00f0licum winde, micel fleogende fugelcyn feorran ofer s\u00e6; \u00fea flugon\nNe ateorode him se mete \u00f0e hi swa micclum gewilnodon, ac \u00fe\u00e6t fl\u00e6sc cleofode \u00fea gyt on heora\nHwi woldon hi gremian God swa un\u00f0earfes, \u00fe\u00e6t hi mid ceorunge forsawon \u00feone mete \u00fee him \u00e6lce\nAnd heora hysecild eac man het acwellan of \u00feam twelf m\u00e6g\u00f0um, \u00fea \u00f0a hi to mannum comon.\nNu alysde hi God of \u00f0am la\u00f0um \u00feeowte, and heora fynd acwealde, and Pharao \u00feone cyning, \u00fee hi swa\nNu w\u00e6ron hi oflyste \u00feurh heora unlustas fl\u00e6sclicra metta, unm\u00e6g\u00f0lice swa\u00feeah, for \u00feam \u00f0e se\nSe heofonlica mete h\u00e6fde \u00fea getacnunge ures H\u00e6lendes Cristes, \u00fee com of heofonum to us, \u00fee is\n\u00deone acwealdon sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t ylce Iudeisce cynn, and noldon hine habban heora sawlum to bigleofan;\nSe \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00e6fter \u00feysum gespr\u00e6c to Moyse \u00feam heretogan, and het hine sendan of \u00f0\u00e6s folces\nMoyses \u00fea genamode of \u00f0am twelf m\u00e6g\u00f0um twelf heafodmenn, and het faran to \u00feam lande, and\nHi ferdon \u00fea sona to \u00f0am fores\u00e6dan lande, and sceawedon \u00feone eard, and eac swylce brohton sume\n\u00d0a wurdon hi ealle wundorlice astyrode mid mycelre ceorunge, and s\u00e6don him betwynan, Uton eft\nIosue, swa\u00feeah, and se snotera Chaleph, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r asende w\u00e6ron mid \u00feam fores\u00e6dum \u00e6rendracan to\nNe beo ge na wi\u00f0err\u00e6de ongean Godes r\u00e6de; ea\u00f0elice we magon \u00fe\u00e6t mancynn ofercuman; ne beo ge\n\u00d0a wurdon hi ealle wundorlice him grame, and woldon hine oftorfian wodlice mid stanum; ac Godes\n\u00c6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra manna \u00fee is of ealre \u00feyssere menigu nu \u00feritigwintre, \u00fee \u00f0us ceorode so\u00f0lice ongean me, ne\nEowre cildra sceolon, \u00f0e nu synd unwittige, habban \u00feone eard \u00fee eow swa mislica\u00f0, and eowre lic\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum wordum wear\u00f0 Godes yrre egeslice geswutelod on \u00f0am \u00e6rendracan \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t land\n\u00d0\u00e6t folc \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6s on merigen macodon hi gearwe, astigon \u00f0a endemys up to anre dune, s\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hi\nHi swa\u00feeah ablende mid gebeote ferdon butan Godes dihte mid dyslicum anginne; ac him com\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum arison eft ongean Moysen \u00feridde healf hund manna mid mycelre ceorunge, \u00fe\u00e6re\nHi axodon \u00f0a mid graman \u00fea Godes \u00feegnas, Moysen and Aaron, Hwi wylle ge swa mycclum eow\nAnd \u00ferafodon hi swy\u00f0e hwi hi sceoldon habban anweald ofer hi.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 moyses him to, nima\u00f0 nu tomerigen eower \u00e6lc his storcyllan, \u00fe\u00e6t ge sterna magon ealle\n\u00d0a \u00fe\u00e6s on merigen wolde Moyses gestillan and mid wisdome alecgan heora wodnysse; sende \u00fea to\nSe Chore \u00fea genam, \u00fee we \u00e6r fores\u00e6don, and ealle his gegadan, Gode to forsewennysse, \u00e6lc his\nMid \u00feam \u00fee hi \u00f0us dydon mid dyrstigon anginne, \u00fea \u00e6tiwde \u00fe\u00e6r sona gesewenlice Godes wuldor, and\nAnd seo eor\u00f0e tob\u00e6rst under heora fotum, and forswealh Dathan for his dyrstignysse, and \u00feone\n\u00d0\u00e6r com eac swylce fyr f\u00e6rlice fram Gode, and forb\u00e6rnde \u00feone Chore \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r he b\u00e6r \u00feone stor, and\nOn \u00feam \u00e6ftran d\u00e6ge \u00fee \u00f0is gedon w\u00e6s, ongan eall \u00fe\u00e6t folc flitan wi\u00f0 moysen, and wi\u00f0 \u00feone aaron \u00fee\nOn \u00f0ysum m\u00e6g gehyran se \u00f0e h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00e6nig andgyt \u00fe\u00e6t hit by\u00f0 swy\u00f0e hearmlic \u00feam \u00f0e huxlice t\u00e6l\u00f0\n\u00d0\u00e6t is on urum gereorde, se \u00fee eow gehyr\u00f0, he gehyr\u00f0 me \u00feurh \u00f0a gehyrsumnysse, and se \u00fee eow\nHi forsawon moysen and \u00feone m\u00e6ron bisceop, aaron his bro\u00f0or, mid bysmorlicum hospe, ac god sylf\nSwa de\u00f0 \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra manna \u00fee his ealdor forsyh\u00f0, \u00fee by\u00f0 godes speligend on gastlicere lare, on \u00feam\nHi w\u00e6ron fl\u00e6sclice menn, and underfencgon heora wite on \u00f0yssere worulde, \u00e6fter moyses \u00e6; we\nEft on o\u00f0rum timan \u00fe\u00e6t israhela folc, \u00fea \u00f0a hi ferdon mid \u00feam fores\u00e6dan moyse, and becomon to \u00f0am\nWe nabba\u00f0 \u00feone hlaf \u00fee us lyste etan, and us nu wlata\u00f0 wi\u00f0 \u00feysne leohtan mete.\n\u00d0a for \u00fe\u00e6re ceorunge sende him god to byrnende n\u00e6ddran, swa swa us bec secga\u00f0, and \u00fea fyrenan\nHi comon \u00fea to moyse, and cw\u00e6don him \u00feus to: we habba\u00f0 gesyngod \u00fe\u00e6t we swa spr\u00e6con ongean\nAnd moyses \u00fea sona geb\u00e6d for \u00feam folce, swa swa hi hine b\u00e6don.\n\u00d0a spr\u00e6c se \u00e6lmihtiga god to \u00feam arwur\u00f0an moysen, hat nu gewyrcan ane \u00e6rene n\u00e6ddran, and gesete\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea moyses het macian \u00fea n\u00e6ddran, and gesettan to tacne, swa swa god sylf hine het, and \u00fea\nSe h\u00e6lend sylf s\u00e6de on sumum his godspelle hw\u00e6t \u00feeos d\u00e6d getacnode on \u00f0am diglan andgyte, and\nWe wylla\u00f0 swa\u00f0eah secgan sceortlice her nu \u00fe\u00e6t seo \u00e6rene n\u00e6ddre, \u00fee butan attre w\u00e6s, h\u00e6fde\n\u00d0a terendan n\u00e6ddran, \u00fee tot\u00e6ron \u00fe\u00e6t folc, syndon ure synna, \u00fee us tosliton wylla\u00f0; ac we sceolon\n\u00d0\u00e6t folc on \u00f0am westene w\u00e6s \u00fea geh\u00e6led \u00feurh \u00f0a \u00e6renan n\u00e6ddran fram \u00feam andweardan dea\u00f0e; ac\nSeo gehiwode anlicnys geh\u00e6lde \u00f0a hwilwendlice, and \u00fe\u00e6t so\u00f0e \u00feing nu syl\u00f0 us \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif.\nGod afandode \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6s folces anr\u00e6dnysse on \u00f0am langsumum f\u00e6relde feowertig geara; he wolde \u00fe\u00e6t hi\n\u00d0a wurdon hi wi\u00f0err\u00e6de wolice foroft, and \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan god swa egeslice gegremedon \u00fe\u00e6t eall\nHi w\u00e6ron gehyrsume godes h\u00e6sum \u00e6fre, and hi for\u00fei h\u00e6fdon \u00feone behatenan eard, and \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t\nFeowertig wintra hi w\u00e6ron on \u00feam westene farende, and moyses geendode eac on \u00feam f\u00e6relde, \u00fea \u00fea\nSeo geogu\u00f0 \u00fee w\u00e6s on \u00feam westene afedd w\u00e6s \u00fea geweaxen, and to wige ful strang, and iosue hi\n\u00d0am folce w\u00e6s behaten \u00feurh \u00feone heofonlican god \u00fe\u00e6t hi sceoldon habban so\u00f0lice renscuras and\nAc crist sylf behet us on his halgan godspelle \u00fe\u00e6t we sceolon habban, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r he sylf wuna\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t ece\nHe het us swy\u00f0ost cepan \u00fe\u00e6s so\u00fean lifes \u00e6fre, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t we sceoldon symle eac habban ure\nPaulus se apostol, ealra \u00feeoda lareow, manode \u00feone leodscipe \u00fee he to geleafan gebigde, and ealle\nHit stent on bocum awriten for ure beterunge, and to mycelre bysne us endenextum mannum, \u00fe\u00e6t we\nNu syndon manega menn \u00fee secga\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hi nella\u00f0 godes lare gehyran, \u00feel\u00e6ste hi sceolon habban\nNu cwe\u00f0e we \u00fe\u00e6rtogeanes, \u00fe\u00e6t gif se cyning asent gewrit to sumon his \u00feegena, and he hit forsyh\u00f0 swa\nSeo halige lar nis na on eallum leodscypum swa swy\u00f0e swa on sumon, ac us secga\u00f0 bec \u00fe\u00e6t hi mihton\nSe man \u00fee h\u00e6f\u00f0 lare on his leodscype genoge, and m\u00e6g \u00f0a gehyran butan micclum geswince, and nele\nSe \u00fee lare n\u00e6f\u00f0, ne lare ne gehyr\u00f0, se mihte habban sume beladunge; ac paulus se apostol cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his\n\u00d0\u00e6t is, on engliscere spr\u00e6ce, \u00f0a \u00fee buton godes \u00e6 synna gewyrca\u00f0, \u00fea eac butan godes \u00e6 on ende\nGerihtl\u00e6ce us se leofa drihten crist, and us gewenie to his willan \u00e6fre, \u00feam is wuldor and lof a to",
